PRIMARY RESOURCE PHASE TRANSITION

The first major H138 result is positive:

EVIDENCE DEMAND
IS A FUNCTION OF
CURRENT ACTIVE VALUE
AND
AUDIT PRICE.

At low current activity:
the family is often left dormant.

At moderate activity:
rising evidence price pushes the organism
from:
family inference
toward:
local-only/defer.

At high activity:
the immediate value of broad resolution
can justify family inference even at high audit price.

Thus:

DORMANT MEMORY
DOES NOT IMPLY
DORMANT COMPUTE.

The organism can retain:
cheap family state

without:
continually paying
to make it current.

DOWNTAIL RESULT

RISK-AWARE has a better 1st-percentile net than FIXED-5
through nearly all:
low-activity
and:
high-price
cells.

Examples:

active 5%, price 8:

RISK:
-7.70.

FIXED-5:
-63.19.

active 10%, price 8:

RISK:
-8.42.

FIXED-5:
-58.99.

active 20%, price 8:

RISK:
-39.19.

FIXED-5:
-52.30.

Thus:
economic defer
is a real tail-risk tool
when active value is sparse.

UNEXPECTED CERTIFICATION RESULT

The preregistered intuition expected certification to occupy an intermediate resource region.

That is only partly correct.

Observed:

CERTIFICATION
BEHAVES LIKE
A CHEAP-EVIDENCE LUXURY.

It appears most strongly when:

- active value is high;
- evidence is cheap;
- enough family-wide value exists to justify buying confidence.

As audit price rises,
the expected-value controller often does NOT:

certify more carefully.

Instead it chooses between:

DEFER
when active value is low

and:

BROADCAST WITHOUT CERTIFICATE
when active value is high.

This creates the central H138 limit.

